From 7c8c69064fd71e5ae0872f7805ee537992cf45ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 08:52:28 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_servers: let the user keep an agent's questions out of
 cards
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Claude Agent (Plus) appends a rule to its system prompt, from 0.39.0, that
steers the model into asking the questions it needs answered through
AskUserQuestion, which Zeo renders as a question card, instead of leaving
them in the reply (Zeo next proposal §6.43, ask 67). The adapter turns the
rule on whenever the client advertises form elicitation, which Zeo does,
so Zeo has nothing to send for the default.

This adds the way out: `agent.ask_questions_in_cards`, true by default, on
the Settings page under Agent Configuration. Set to false, every session
request -- `session/new`, `session/load`, `session/resume`, over v1 and v2
-- carries `_meta: { "askQuestionsInCards": false }`, and the adapter
leaves its prompt as the preset. Only the opt-out is sent: at the default
every agent receives the request it received before, so no other agent
sees a key it does not know.

The value is read when the request is built, not when the connection is
made, so a thread reopened after the change follows it. One limit sits in
Claude Code, not here: it records the system prompt once per conversation,
so a resumed conversation keeps the prompt it started with until the next
compaction.

`session_meta.rs` reads the merged settings through `try_global`, because
agent_servers does not depend on agent_settings and a test app may run
without a settings store. Tests: the key and its absence
(`session_meta`), the v2 wire for new and resume
(`v2_session_requests_carry_the_question_card_opt_out`), and the v1 wire
for new, load and resume (`question_cards_meta_tests`), whose harness, from
0036, now records the three session requests. Red seen: with the v1 load
wiring removed, the v1 test fails.
---

